{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Behold, I.</b> In the merit of the Ten Commandments, which begin with 'I' — 'I am sending a messenger before you to guard you.' Another explanation: the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: 'Behold, I.' Moses said to Him: 'I do not ask for a messenger to go with us, but You in Your glory. And if Your Shekhinah does not go with us, we are not moving from here.' The Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: 'Even a messenger I am not sending, but only the hornet, as it is written: ״וגם את הצרעה״.' And specifically in this world He sends the hornet, but in the future to come: 'Behold, I' — He sends you Elijah the prophet, as it is said: ״הנה אנכי שולח לכם את אליה הנביא״. Thus it is written: ״הנה אנכי שולח לכם מלאך״."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "The final scriptural citation 'הנה אנכי שולח לכם מלאך' appears to be the same verse (Exodus 23:20) restated as a prooftext; the note's chain of interpretations moves from literal to midrashic readings of 'הנה אנכי.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:04:00.806554998Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}